# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58) and L §8: a load refusal in a scenario file refuses only that scenario, so the
# reality loads (its base answers, L8_3_scenario_load_refusal_base), and `REQ-ASK` is checked after it. The request
# names zz, which no file declares: the run prints the one refusal, "nothing else", so the scenario's own refusal line
# doesn't print. Was that line (`scenario bad: refused: LOAD-DUP …`, exit 0) and the load's warning, zz skipped.
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
source s "synthetic"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
ask q: minor(DUK)
=== bad.tally
scenario bad over f
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01
def q: int = 1
ask qx: q in bad
=== expect zz
refused: REQ-ASK no ask zz
